## Adding Window Animations to Fedora i3 with picom-ftlabs

### 1. Fix the i3 config typo
In `~/.config/i3/config`, the last line had `:wq` accidentally appended:
```
for_window [class="Wine"] floating enable   # removed the :wq
```

### 2. Install build dependencies
```bash
sudo dnf install -y meson ninja-build xcb-util-devel libev-devel \
  xcb-util-renderutil-devel xcb-util-image-devel libconfig-devel \
  dbus-devel pcre2-devel uthash-devel libXext-devel libXdamage-devel \
  libXfixes-devel libXcomposite-devel libXrandr-devel libXrender-devel \
  pixman-devel libepoxy-devel
```

### 3. Clone and build picom-ftlabs
```bash
git clone https://github.com/FT-Labs/picom ~/builds/picom-ftlabs
cd ~/builds/picom-ftlabs
meson setup --buildtype=release build
ninja -C build
sudo ninja -C build install
```

### 4. Configure animations
Create/edit `~/.config/picom/picom.conf` and add:
```conf
animations = true;
animation-stiffness = 200;
animation-dampening = 25;
animation-mass = 1;

animation-for-open-window = "zoom";
animation-for-unmap-window = "zoom";
animation-for-workspace-switch-in = "slide-right";
animation-for-workspace-switch-out = "slide-left";
```

### 5. Update i3 config to use the config file explicitly
In `~/.config/i3/config`:
```
exec_always --no-startup-id picom --config ~/.config/picom/picom.conf -b
```

### 6. Restart i3
```
$mod+Shift+r
```

---

Note: the stock `picom v13` that ships with Fedora has no animation support — picom-ftlabs is a fork that adds it, which is why the custom build was necessary.
